ext","title":"Press Note: Interim Agreement Signed","paras":["After eleven months, the council and the dockworkers have signed an interim agreement. By next spring they **will have been trading** concessions for a year and a half. The union **endorsed** the pay review; the council **agreed to** a phased timetable, **and to** safety audits. “We **took on** a hard case,” said the mediator. “Weakness in mandates **gave rise to** mistrust, but both sides **held firm** on principle.”","Whether the deal lasts, no one can say; whether it should, many **can**."],"kicker":"PRESS NOTE","by":"Port Authority","gloss":[["dockworker","estivador"],["audit","auditoria"],["interim","provisório"],["principle","princípio"]]}]},{"tag":"Compreensão","title":"Did you understand?","blocks":[{"type":"tfng","title":"","items":[{"q":"The agreement is final.","ans":"F","why":"interim."},{"q":"The council accepted a phased timetable.","ans":"T","why":"agreed to a phased timetable."},{"q":"Mistrust came from weak mandates.","ans":"T","why":"weakness in mandates."}]},{"type":"mcq","title":"Vocabulary in context","items":[{"q":"“endorse” = ?","opts":["endossar","desdobrar","dominar"],"ans":0,"why":"endorse."},{"q":"“audit” = ?","opts":["auditoria","audição","anúncio"],"ans":0,"why":"audit = auditoria."}]}]},{"tag":"Gramática","title":"Grammar recap","blocks":[{"type":"table","head":["Verifique","Exemplo"],"rows":[["Uso **will have been + -ing** para duração?","By spring they **will have been trading** for a year."],["Uso **give rise to** com sujeito = causa?","Weak mandates **gave rise to** mistrust."],["Omito **sem ambiguidade** (elipse)?","The union agreed to X, the council **to** Y."],["Sinalizo uma **apresentação**?","**That brings me to** …"],["Uso **hold** e **take on**?","**hold firm**; **take on** a case"]],"cap":"Autoavaliação da Unidade 11"}]},{"tag":"Prática","title":"Practice · Mixed review","blocks":[{"type":"gap","title":"Complete the sentences (from the unit)","bank":null,"items":[